  "attestation": "D-133 closed-loop round 9 fixes on needs-wording (audit of 0fca6cb: 1 HIGH, 2 MEDIUM, 8 LOW). HIGH-1: applyChanges keys each recorded answer and every host-answer marker on item|changesetId|question (answerKey), since Alembic gives every answer of one digest the digest's own item (agent-endpoint.ts changes); every answer of a digest is recorded, an asked-again or refused marker never stands for a sibling. Also in v1.0.5; no migration: old markers carry all three fields, skipped answers were never recorded, so the next apply records them and a re-export re-asks them (tested). MEDIUM-1: wordEntry marks a question gone (no choices, unseen, GONE detail) when a unit it names is not in the text, for every kind except a removal of the instructor's text. MEDIUM-2: exportNeeds ranks every cluster (buildDigest cap Infinity), splits, takes questions round robin over clusters, and applies the instructor's cap in questions. LOW-1: apply requires words for DIGEST_CHOICES and BINDING_KINDS choices except Later whatever the record says. LOW-2: buildDigest reads Later on key#finding (laterFindings, laterBefore), the split question goes first and only it is marked; overflow says it waited. LOW-3: split when any finding has choices. LOW-4: singular chapter. LOW-5: left counts questions; hand-in digest.remaining (additive, documented in alembic-job/CLAUDE.md; Alembic adoption separate). LOW-6: sources named by FOUNDATION title, plain rights words; unknown plan node said by kind and words. LOW-7: evidence lists include audit8 and audit9. LOW-8: bindingContext built once per apply run. Tests: tests/needs-wording.audit9.test.mjs (13, all failing on 0fca6cb); two expectations in alembic-needs-wording.test.mjs follow LOW-6 and MEDIUM-1. Full suite 1284/1284 passed (--test-concurrency=2).",
